---
import RecordingLibrary from '../RecordingLibrary.astro';
---

<section id="cases" class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2>05 Case studies</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The selected comparisons illustrate three conclusions. In-context learning (ICL) guides
        task-specific manipulation. Task-level adaptation does not guarantee precise execution.
        Atomic task execution does not guarantee compositional completion. The teacup and glasses
        recordings reveal <strong>complementary capabilities</strong>: GPT-6-Astra revises grasps
        and recovers disrupted goals, while specialized policies execute fine manipulation more
        accurately in these examples. This separate compositional-completion experiment also reports
        10-rollout success rates and scores.
      </p>
    </div>
    <section id="case-icl" class="case-study-section" aria-labelledby="case-icl-title">
      <h3 id="case-icl-title">In-context learning</h3>
      <div class="case-study-content"></div>
    </section>
    <section id="case-adapt" class="case-study-section" aria-labelledby="case-adapt-title">
      <h3 id="case-adapt-title">Adaptation and precision</h3>
      <div class="case-study-content"></div>
    </section>
    <section id="case-poc" class="case-study-section" aria-labelledby="case-poc-title">
      <h3 id="case-poc-title">Compositional completion</h3>
      <div class="case-study-content"></div>
    </section>
    <RecordingLibrary />
  </div>
</section>
